From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:55:49 +0800
Subject: app/timeline: reopen a session where it was left after a reload

Like Telegram: the row at the top of the viewport (timeline key, with the turn
as fallback, and the offset into it) is saved per session in localStorage
shortly after scrolling and when the page hides; following the newest content
saves "at the bottom". After a reload (iOS discarding the page, a new tab)
the timeline loads older pages down to that turn and restores the row and
offset. In-app session switches keep their live views as before.

Ocelot-Patch: web/timeline-position

